This extension adds State of Decay 2 modding support to Vortex Mod Manager.

[b][size=3][color=#ea9999]IMPORTANT - This extension cannot directly install "Integration" pak mods that require the [/color][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/stateofdecay2/mods/96]SoD2 Mod Manager[/url][color=#ea9999]. Note that if you run SoD2 MM while Vortex pak mods are deployed, it will forcibly rename the .pak files. This breaks the symlink/hardlink deployment of Vortex and will generate an "External Changes" popup. You can deal with this in one of the ways below.[/color]
[/size][/b][b][size=3][color=#a4c2f4]Either way, you can download all mods through Vortex and then choose one of the above options for Integration Mods[/color][/size]
[color=#ffff00]A. If you want to use Integration Mods without impacting your Vortex pak mod deployment, simply Purge mods in Vortex, then install mods with SoD2 MM, then Deploy mods in Vortex again. This will avoid files being forcibly renamed. [/color]
[size=3][color=#b6d7a8]B. You can just let SoD2 MM go ahead and rename the pak files after installing with Vortex and accept the External Changes popup. [/color][/size][/b]

[b]✅ Supported Versions:[/b]
[list]
[*]Steam[/*]
[*]Epic[/*]
[*]Xbox[/*]
[*]Other versions may need to select the installation location manually.[/*]
[/list]
[b]🛠️ Mod Installation Notes:[/b]
[list]
[*]UE4SS Script-LogicMod Combo mods with both a "Content" and a "Binaries" folder install to the "StateOfDecay2" folder.[/*]
[*]UE Sortable Pak mods with a ".pak" file install to the "%LOCALAPPDATA%\StateOfDecay2\Saved\Paks" folder.[/*]
[*]Root Folder mods with a top-level folder such as "StateOfDecay2", "Engine" or "Content" install to the game folder.[/*]
[*]Config (Local AppData) mods with a config file such as "engine.ini" or "game.ini" install to the game's config folder.[/*]
[*]Saves (Local AppData) mods with a ".sav" file install to the game's save folder.[/*]
[*]Cooked mods with a "Cooked" folder install to the "{localAppData}\StateOfDecay2\Saved" folder.[/*]
[*]SoD2 Mod Manager installs to the game folder, recognised by a "modintegrator.exe" file.[/*]
[*]Any other mod not described above installs to the "StateOfDecay2\Binaries\Win64" folder ("WinGDK" instead of "Win64" for the Xbox version).[/*]
[*]Archives with a FOMOD installer (a "fomod" folder with ModuleConfig.xml) are handed to Vortex's built-in FOMOD installer instead.[/*]
[/list]
[b]📋 Usage Notes:[/b]
[list]
[*]You can open several useful files/folders/URLs using the buttons within the folder icon on the Mods toolbar.[/*]
[*]Pak mods are sorted on the "Load Order" page. Pak mods placed by a FOMOD installer show up there too.[/*]
[*]Config and Save mods only work if the game, the mod staging folder and the config/save folder are all on the same drive (limitation of hardlinks). Vortex shows a notification when they are not.[/*]
[*]For upscalers, reshades, and other mods that need to be next to the game executable, please use the "Binaries (Engine Injector)" mod type. This is the fallback mod install location if no other installer is triggered.[/*]
[*]Automatically installs .pak mods to the correct folder and adds them to the Load Order tab. If the mod contains multiple .pak files, you will get a popup to pick which files you want to install.[/*]
[/list]

[b]📝 Notes for Mod Authors:[/b]
[spoiler]
Packaging rules for State of Decay 2 mods, so Vortex installs them to the right place.

Vortex decides what a mod is by looking at the files and folders inside the archive. It tries each installer in order and the first one that matches wins, so archive layout is what determines where your mod ends up.

========================================================================

Combo Mods (pak + UE4SS script/DLL together):

Use this layout when one download ships both game content and UE4SS mods. It is recognised by the presence of BOTH a "Content" folder and a "Binaries" folder, laid out exactly as they appear inside the game folder.

[code]
MyComboMod.zip
├── Content\
│   └── Paks\
│       └── LogicMods\
│           └── MyBlueprintMod.pak
└── Binaries\
    └── Win64\
        └── ue4ss\
            └── Mods\
                └── MyScriptMod\
                    └── Scripts\
                        └── main.lua
[/code]

  Requirements:
    - Both a "Content" folder and a "Binaries" folder must be present, or this installer is skipped.
    - Mirror the real in-game folder structure below those two folders.
    - This installer is tested before the individual pak/script/DLL installers, so a matching archive is always handled as a combo.

  Installs to: "StateOfDecay2"

  Common mistakes:
    - Including only one of "Content" or "Binaries" - the archive then falls through to a different installer.
    - Adding an extra wrapper folder between "Binaries" and "Win64".

========================================================================

Pak Mods:

Standard content mods: one or more ".pak" files. Vortex copies just the pak files themselves, flattened, so the folder structure around them does not matter.

[code]
MyPakMod.zip
└── MyPakMod.pak
[/code]

  Requirements:
    - Any archive containing a ".pak" file reaches this installer (unless an earlier one claimed it).
    - Only the pak files are installed - surrounding folders are discarded.
    - If the archive holds more than one pak, Vortex asks the user which to install - useful for optional variants.

  Installs to: "%LOCALAPPDATA%\StateOfDecay2\Saved\Paks"

  Common mistakes:
    - Shipping several unrelated paks in one archive when you meant them all to install - the user gets a choice dialog and may pick only one.
    - Blueprint mods belong in a "LogicMods" folder instead - see above.

========================================================================

Root / Game Folder Mods:

For mods that replace or add files inside the game installation, laid out the same way they appear in the game folder.

[code]
MyRootMod.zip
└── StateOfDecay2\
    └── ... files in their real relative locations
[/code]

  Requirements:
    - Recognised by a top-level folder matching any of: "StateOfDecay2", "Engine", "Content", "Binaries", "Mods", "Paks" or "Movies".
    - The matched folder and everything below it is copied into the game folder, preserving structure.

  Installs to: the game folder

  Common mistakes:
    - Zipping the folder that CONTAINS the game folders instead of the game folders themselves adds an extra level and misplaces every file.

========================================================================

Config File Mods:

Config tweaks are deployed to the game's config folder in your user profile, not into the game installation.

  Requirements:
    - Recognised by any of these filenames in the archive: "engine.ini", "game.ini", "gameusersettings.ini", "input.ini", "scalability.ini", "hardware.ini", "deviceprofiles.ini", "compat.ini", "runtimeoptions.ini", "gameplaytags.ini", "enhancedinput.ini" or "consolevariables.ini".

  Common mistakes:
    - Shipping a config file with one of these names inside an unrelated mod - the whole archive is then treated as a config mod.

========================================================================

Save Game Files:

Save files are deployed to the game's save folder in your user profile.

  Requirements:
    - Recognised by any file with extension ".sav".

  Common mistakes:
    - Including an example save alongside a normal mod - the archive is then treated as a save, not a mod.

========================================================================

Cooked:

Recognised when the archive contains a "Cooked" folder.

  Installs to: "{localAppData}\StateOfDecay2\Saved"

========================================================================

Modmanager:

Recognised when the archive contains a "modintegrator.exe" file.

  Installs to: the game folder

========================================================================

Fallback Installer:

This is the catch-all. Any archive with no ".pak" file that matched none of the installers above lands here and is copied, unchanged, into the game's binaries folder.

[b][color=#ffff00]NOTE: Landing in the fallback installer is a signal your archive layout needs fixing.[/color][/b]

  Requirements:
    - Reaching this installer usually means the archive was not laid out in a way Vortex recognised.
    - Vortex shows the user a notification when a mod installs through the fallback.

  Installs to: "StateOfDecay2\Binaries\Win64" ("WinGDK" instead of "Win64" for the Xbox version)

  Common mistakes:
    - If your mod lands here unintentionally, re-check the layouts above - users will see a fallback warning and may report it as broken.

========================================================================

Rules That Apply To Every Mod Type:

    - Archives containing a FOMOD installer (a "fomod" folder with ModuleConfig.xml) are handed to the built-in FOMOD installer instead.
    - Folder and file name matching is case-insensitive.
    - Extra wrapper folders around a recognised folder are generally fine.
[/spoiler]

